WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.149
I’ve never made like a big dick line in
any of my songs.

00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:04.330
That was my first one.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.600
‘Cause like I’m not on some like micro
shit.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.100
You know what I mean?

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.780
But like I’m also like not crazy…

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.600
You know what I’m saying?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.020
But I was so worried that the girls I used to
mess with were gonna be like...

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:14.940
“Song’s hard."

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.320
"But just know like…"

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.080
"It ain’t that big.”

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.940
Nobody said nothing so we’re in the clear.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.950
Maybe they’re like, “It was…”

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:25.120
Like maybe they think I’m telling the truth.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:25.720
I don’t know.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:27.680
Next line bruh.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:35.680
Clipse.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.659
‘Hell Hath No Fury.’

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.771
“We Got It For Cheap.”

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:38.560
It’s the intro.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.040
We had been listening to Clipse all week.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.660
Me and my producer, 2forwOyNE.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.280
And I played him that one.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.900
As soon as we got to the studio, that was
the immediate influence.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.460
Everybody been noticing that, saying, “Oh
this sounds just like ‘We Got It For Cheap.’”

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.120
Definitely.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.220
It’s totally paying homage.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.140
Let me start off by saying, what’s crazy
about this record is all growing up, I was

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.219
never into drugs or drinking.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.020
All through high school.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:06.520
I didn’t do it.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.760
I just wasn’t that intrigued.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.979
And then I remember, the summer after I graduated,
a big group of my friends were doing that

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.590
and it was the first thing that ever made
me like, “Dang."

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:16.780
"I wanna do that.”

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.280
So one night, I just did it with them and
this is before I smoked or drank ever.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.780
It’s like the first drug I ever did.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.380
It was a trip for sure.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.460
I was feeling fly that day.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.171
Not everyday you feel fly but that day I was
feeling like, “I feel like a pimp.”

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.000
Like I just feel like I was on some cool shit.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.040
Everybody in Louisville likes Big Red, likes
Grippos.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.700
It’s like a signature soda from where we’re
from.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:58.189
A lot of people have never ever heard of the
drink but to us, it might as well be a Pepsi.

00:01:58.189 --> 00:01:58.700
You know what I mean?

00:01:58.940 --> 00:01:59.600
It’s a major soda.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.320
Private Garden, the collective.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.631
A lot of 
fellas like we ain’t even got cars so a

00:02:16.631 --> 00:02:17.890
